  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies_finish.rs` no longer cuts the Z span of the sample into 6 equal bands.\n- The span is now measured in 48 equal parts from the model's top. The table `EDGES` gives 12 bands: `0, 26, 29, 30, 32, 33, 35, 37, 39, 41, 43, 45, 48`.\n- The upper band (0..26) holds the fast upper half. Below the half, each band is 1 to 3 parts deep.\n- The heavy band tests go from 6 to 12. The `#[test]` count of the file goes from 8 to 15.\n- The assert body of each band (`the_3d_finish_band_generates_with_no_gouge`) does not change. Each band still asserts generate `ok`, the full verify gate, no gouge, `gate.ok`, the blocking `shank_hit`, `ok == false` and `held_by == [\"S1\"]`.\n- A new default-suite test, `the_3d_finish_bands_are_narrow_where_the_levels_are_slow`, keeps the table narrow in the slow half. It also keeps the top band at the model's top.\n- A `const` assert keeps the `band!` list and `EDGES` in step.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3513-reband-shared-face-finish.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe generate time per level is not even over the span. The lower half of the sample holds almost all of it. The time is also not additive in the band depth. Old band 4 took 559 s alone, but its eight 1/48 parts took 247 s together. The time depends on where the level ladder of each band falls. So the edges come from measured bands.\n\n## Readings (release, host with 32 cores, each band alone)\n\nEach band ran alone, one after the other, in one process. The work is the same as the band test: `sample_job`, `edit_operation`, `generate`, `verify`. A temporary probe took the readings. The probe is not in the PR.\n\nBefore (6 equal bands):\n\n| Band | Parts of 48 | Time (s) |\n|---|---|---:|\n| 1 | 0..8 | 12.1 |\n| 2 | 8..16 | 7.4 |\n| 3 | 16..24 | 13.0 |\n| 4 | 24..32 | 558.9 |\n| 5 | 32..40 | 162.0 |\n| 6 | 40..48 | 217.8 |\n\nSlowest / fastest: 75x. Sum: 971 s.\n\nAfter (12 bands):\n\n| Band | Parts of 48 | Time (s) |\n|---|---|---:|\n| 1 | 0..26 | 48.5 |\n| 2 | 26..29 | 59.2 |\n| 3 | 29..30 | 46.5 |\n| 4 | 30..32 | 53.5 |\n| 5 | 32..33 | 44.0 |\n| 6 | 33..35 | 56.7 |\n| 7 | 35..37 | 53.4 |\n| 8 | 37..39 | 35.4 (first run 103.1, see below) |\n| 9 | 39..41 | 67.3 |\n| 10 | 41..43 | 58.7 |\n| 11 | 43..45 | 51.4 |\n| 12 | 45..48 | 71.5 |\n\nSlowest / fastest: 2.0x. Sum: 646 s.\n\nThe host was loaded (load average 21-30) during the readings. Band 8 read 103.1 s on the first run and 35.4 s on a re-run, with the same code. The other readings can also move by that amount.\n\nWall time of the whole heavy step (all bands in one process at the same time):\n\n- Before: 564.5 s (6 bands, probe run).\n- After: 70.6 s (`cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: shared_face_bodies_finish\"`, `--test-threads=32`).\n\nThe 1/48 parts 0..3 at the model's top have no `shank_hit` finding. So the top band must start at the top and must be deep.\n\n## Tests (on the final head)\n\n- Pin: `the_3d_finish_bands_are_narrow_where_the_levels_are_slow`.\n  - Red on unchanged code: `band 1 in the fast upper half starts at the model's top`.\n  - Mutation 1, `EDGES` as equal twelfths: red, same message.\n  - Mutation 2, last band 44..48 (4 parts): red, `band 11 in the slow lower half is too wide`.\n  - Restored: green.\n- `the_3d_finish_bands_tile_the_whole_span`: green (not changed).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base HEAD` on the final tree before the commit (the diff of this PR): `app suites: shared_face_bodies_finish` ok (3 passed, 12 ignored).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --only \"app suites: example_catalog\"`: ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy step `app heavy: shared_face_bodies_finish` (release, `--ignored`), 1 step:\n  - on the branch head `efd49acdc`: ok, 12 passed, 70.6 s;\n  - on a trial merge with upstream/main `c2fd4fe62`: ok, 12 passed, 64.3 s.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff is one test file and one decision file. No recorded program (`*.nc`, `*.cl`, `examples/catalog/**`) can change. The example catalog suite ran and is green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No readings from the cut runner. The edges come from one host. A different host can move an edge by one part.\n- No light twin. The issue does not ask for one.\n- The generate time of old band 4 (559 s against 247 s for its parts) can be a performance defect in the 3D Finish level ladder. This PR does not examine it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies_finish.rs`.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: none (test only)\n\nFixes #3513\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
